   "MonsterInfo_320000680_DiscoveredDes": "This enemy has a <color=HighlightB>higher RES</color> to <color=Ice>Glacio DMG</color>.\n\nWhen enemies nearby obtain a shield, Forbidden Bastion takes 10% more total DMG for 6s. This effect can be triggered once every 0.5s, stacking up to 4 times.\n\nEvery brick and tile in the Censure Court is made of modular parts. It is both an elegant garden and a prison for holding and purging Tacet Discords.\nWithin the Censure Court, the Forbidden Bastion is one of the most formidable Autopuppets. The columns and ridges within the Court form its towering build.\nThe ultimate defense that safeguards the grounds, Forbidden Bastion spends year after year purging the Tacet Discords left behind within these walls, maintaining peace within Xuanfang.",
   "MonsterInfo_320000680_Name": "Forbidden Bastion",
   "MonsterInfo_320000680_UndiscoveredDes": "Within the Censure Court lies an Autopuppet hailed as the Censure Court's Apparatus.\" Legends tell it bears an enormous form and is especially formidable in strength.",
-  "MonsterInfo_320000690_DiscoveredDes": "This enemy has a <color=HighlightB>higher RES</color> to <color=Wind>Areo DMG</color>.\nThe total Negative Status DMG taken by this enemy is increased by 100%.\n\nA type of Autopuppet developed by the Court of Savantae in Mengzhou to counter airborne Tacet Discords. Its exceptional mobility is designed for rapid deployment, enabling it to provide emergency support to Censure Courts across the region.\n\nIts design draws inspiration from the Xuanling Bird. The propulsion units mounted on either side employ the same levitation technology used in the Skywatch Ring.\n\nUnfortunately, before the Skywatch Lancer could enter large-scale production at Skyworks, the manufacturing lines were destroyed by Tacet Discords during the Fortress and Gorges War.",
+  "MonsterInfo_320000690_DiscoveredDes": "This enemy has a <color=HighlightB>higher RES</color> to <color=Wind>Aero DMG</color>.\nThe total Negative Status DMG taken by this enemy is increased by 100%.\n\nA type of Autopuppet developed by the Court of Savantae in Mengzhou to counter airborne Tacet Discords. Its exceptional mobility is designed for rapid deployment, enabling it to provide emergency support to Censure Courts across the region.\n\nIts design draws inspiration from the Xuanling Bird. The propulsion units mounted on either side employ the same levitation technology used in the Skywatch Ring.\n\nUnfortunately, before the Skywatch Lancer could enter large-scale production at Skyworks, the manufacturing lines were destroyed by Tacet Discords during the Fortress and Gorges War.",
   "MonsterInfo_320000690_Name": "Skywatch Lancer",
   "MonsterInfo_320000690_UndiscoveredDes": "Clad in steel feather armor, wielding a lance. It excels at proving covering firing from the sky. But its existence seems to only be found in the historical records of the Land of Xuanfang.",
   "MonsterInfo_320000700_DiscoveredDes": "This enemy has a <color=HighlightB>higher RES</color> to <color=Fire>Fusion DMG</color>.\n\nHaving seized part of Hsin's authority, Suhsin the Inevitable replicated Hsin's method for making Kernel Puppets and built one solely for war, the Formrender.\n\nThey tear into Autopuppets and raid repair workshops again and again, cutting down the Celestials' Artisan Autopuppets to stall the Civilization Capsule's restoration.\n\nTo enhance their capabilities even further, Suhsin the Inevitable poured in the fervor and rage that saturate the Heart of Flames. The Formrenders became more powerful but steadily slid into chaos and frenzy, until even their Kernels were twisted along with them.",
@@ -283908,7 +283908,7 @@
   "Side_XZQTCHJ_29_3": "...Did she give in to it?",
   "Side_XZQTCHJ_29_4": "I wasn't there to witness what happened in the end. But it's possible. She was always one to be easily swayed.",
   "Side_XZQTCHJ_2_1": "Ren Water runs through the rivers, softening Metal Chi. Gui Water rises to the Heavenly Stems, surging out over the world.  But look at the way this mountain leans—Ren Water can't run clean, and the Metal Chi's all backed up...",
-  "Side_XZQTCHJ_2_10": "My master once taught me Chinese Geomancy and Chi Observation Arts. At first, I figured Fengshui wouldn't apply inside the Simulacrum Nexus, and I felt sorry about letting all that teaching go to waste.",
+  "Side_XZQTCHJ_2_10": "My master once taught me Geomancy and Chi Observation Arts. At first, I figured Fengshui wouldn't apply inside the Simulacrum Nexus, and I felt sorry about letting all that teaching go to waste.",
   "Side_XZQTCHJ_2_11": "Then a few years back, I discovered the terrain here mirrors the very contours of fate itself. See the clouds and mist hanging frozen over the peak? That's Metal Chi converging. And I'm afraid the cause is... <color=Highlight>warfare</color>.",
   "Side_XZQTCHJ_2_12": "I asked Lady Hsin about it once. She told us not to go poking around. Said we'd fall prey to its baleful Chi. She said that when the time came, an outsider would arrive and set it right—",
